WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.079 --> 00:00:04.200
What is the Multiannual Financial Framework?

00:00:04.479 --> 00:00:06.360
Often referred to as MFF,

00:00:06.519 --> 00:00:08.239
it may sound complicated

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.079
but it is simply the EU's long-term budget

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:13.239
It stretches over several years

00:00:13.439 --> 00:00:17.479
and funds complex programmes
such as Erasmus and Galileo.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:21.839
The MFF determines the amounts
that match the EU's priorities.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.519
This in turn ensures stability.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:28.839
The MFF also sets limits on how much
the European Union will spend

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.519
and in which areas.

00:00:30.759 --> 00:00:34.319
The main EU institutions
all work to shape the MFF:

00:00:34.759 --> 00:00:39.000
EU leaders, who meet in the European
Council to provide political guidance

00:00:39.319 --> 00:00:41.400
and the Commission,
the Council and the Parliament

00:00:41.519 --> 00:00:43.319
that complete the process

00:00:44.319 --> 00:00:45.800
How does the process work?

00:00:46.639 --> 00:00:48.759
The Commission makes the initial proposal

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:52.519
Then it's up to the Council,
which has a central role

00:00:52.959 --> 00:00:56.360
it ensures all EU countries
are part of the agreement.

00:00:56.639 --> 00:01:00.000
Next, the Parliament
is asked to give its consent.

00:01:00.239 --> 00:01:03.439
Once it does so,
the Council adopts the MFF

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:05.439
through an unanimous vote.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:09.400
Find out all you need to know about the MFF

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:13.800
and much more on consilium.europa.eu.

